  "name": "FATTY ACIDS WITH VERY LONG CHAINS C22 TO C26 PLASMA",
  "code": "1085",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"153\" data-end=\"422\">This test measures the concentration of <strong data-start=\"193\" data-end=\"233\">very long-chain fatty acids (VLCFAs)</strong> in the plasma, specifically chains <strong data-start=\"269\" data-end=\"296\">C22:0, C24:0, and C26:0</strong>. These fatty acids are typically broken down in <strong data-start=\"345\" data-end=\"360\">peroxisomes</strong>, and elevated levels can indicate a <strong data-start=\"397\" data-end=\"421\">peroxisomal disorder</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"450\"><strong data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"450\">Clinical uses include:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"843\">\n<li data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"579\">\n<p data-start=\"454\" data-end=\"579\">Diagnosis of <strong data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"508\">X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy (X-ALD)</strong> &ndash; a genetic disorder affecting the adrenal glands and nervous system</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"580\" data-end=\"673\">\n<p data-start=\"582\" data-end=\"673\">Screening for <strong data-start=\"596\" data-end=\"632\">peroxisomal biogenesis disorders</strong> (e.g., <strong data-start=\"640\" data-end=\"672\">Zellweger spectrum disorders</strong>)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"674\" data-end=\"764\">\n<p data-start=\"676\" data-end=\"764\">Evaluation of <strong data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"720\">neurodegenerative symptoms</strong> or <strong data-start=\"724\" data-end=\"749\">adrenal insufficiency</strong> in young males</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"765\" data-end=\"843\">\n<p data-start=\"767\" data-end=\"843\">Follow-up in patients with suggestive <strong data-start=\"805\" data-end=\"821\">MRI findings</strong> or <strong data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"843\">family history</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"843\">Elevated Levels &ndash; Clinical Implications</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Explanation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy (X-ALD)</strong></td>\n<td>Most common cause; due to mutations in the <strong>ABCD1</strong> gene leading to VLCFA buildup in tissues</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Zellweger spectrum disorders</strong></td>\n<td>Group of rare inherited conditions with defective peroxisome formation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Neonatal adrenoleukodystrophy</strong></td>\n<td>A severe form of peroxisomal disorder seen in infants</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Refsum disease (rare)</strong></td>\n<td>A peroxisomal disorder that may also involve abnormal fatty acid metabolism</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
